{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"GHSA-22rm-wp4x-v5cx","published":"2026-03-26T09:30:28Z","modified":"2026-07-15T20:15:16.135540341Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-4874"],"related":["CGA-4gx6-j35v-22q2"],"summary":"Keycloak Server-Side Request Forgery via OIDC token endpoint manipulation","details":"A flaw was found in Keycloak. An authenticated attacker can perform Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) by manipulating the `client_session_host` parameter during refresh token requests. This occurs when a Keycloak client is configured to use the `backchannel.logout.url` with the `application.session.host` placeholder. Successful exploitation allows the attacker to make HTTP requests from the Keycloak server’s network context, potentially probing internal networks or internal APIs, leading to information disclosure.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.keycloak:keycloak-services","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.keycloak/keycloak-services"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"26.5.0"},{"fixed":"26.6.3"}]}],"versions":["26.5.0","26.5.1","26.5.2","26.5.3","26.5.4","26.5.5","26.5.6","26.5.7","26.6.0","26.6.1","26.6.2"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/03/GHSA-22rm-wp4x-v5cx/GHSA-22rm-wp4x-v5cx.json"}},{"package":{"name":"org.keycloak:keycloak-services","ecosystem":"Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.keycloak/keycloak-services"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"26.4.13"}]}],"versions":["1.0-alpha-1","1.0-alpha-1-12062013","1.0-alpha-2","1.0-alpha-3","1.0-alpha-4","1.0-beta-1","1.0-beta-1-20150521","1.0-beta-1-20150523","1.0-beta-2","1.0-beta-3","1.0-beta-4","1.0-final","1.0-rc-1","1.0-rc-2","1.0.1.Final","1.0.2.Final","1.0.3.Final","1.0.4.Final","1.0.5.Final","1.1.0.Beta1","1.1.0.Beta2","1.1.0.Final","1.1.1.Final","1.2.0.Beta1","1.2.0.CR1","1.2.0.Final","1.3.0.Final","1.3.1.Final","1.4.0.Final","1.5.0-Final","1.5.0.Final","1.5.1.Final","1.6.0.Fina